listen closely it's very important that  you pay attention to the visuals you're  seeing and the words you're hearing you  may think you've heard this story before  you get that funny feeling deja vu but  trust me this is all very much new to  you this is the story of a dangerous  species of anomalous creature dubbed  scp-939 also known as with many voices  on october 28 1981 it all started with  an scp foundation field agent going  missing while on duty the whole case had  smelled like death from the beginning on  the edge of an undisclosed city in an  undisclosed american state civilians had  been going missing in unusually high  numbers this would be a concerning state  of affairs in and of itself but things  went up a notch when law enforcement  operatives sent to investigate them  disappeared too disappearances are hard  enough to cover up law enforcement  disappearances are a nightmare if only  it stopped there when the foundation  agent went missing alarm bells were  ringing across the entire district what  the hell kind of threat could take out  civilians trained law enforcement  officers and even foundation operatives  naturally the next step in this  escalation of force was to dispatch a  heavily armed and well-prepared tactical  security force known as trapper from the  nearest foundation containment site  these were six of the best tactical  operators from the sector whatever it  was that killed or took out the others  it wouldn't do the same to them or at  least not all of them the team breached  an abandoned multi-level warehouse on  the edge of town based on the estimated  points of disappearances for the various  victims it was the most feasible  location of an anomalous threat they  used explosive charges to enter the  building and stormed in assault rifles  and submachine guns blazing the team  split up to search different parts of  the complex in a move that even the  mystery gang could tell you doesn't  often work out well though many  scooby-doo episodes might have played  out differently if shaggy was wielding a  heckler and coke  hk416 it didn't take long for the  overpowering stenches of death and decay  to assail the team's nostrils they'd  work for the scp foundation for long  enough to know the distinctive sickly  sweet aroma of rotting human flesh from  memory with heightened awareness they  continued through the building searching  for the source of that awful smell a  member of the team radioed in when they  made the first grisly discovery the  corpse of a missing foundation field  agent killed by what seemed to be one  huge bite taking a fatal chunk from his  neck some kind of animalistic beast had  taken his life in a single decisive  strike once again the danger level had  elevated for the trapper team but it was  about to get a whole lot worse for all  of them some of the team that had split  to check the upper floors of the  warehouse suddenly heard the most  terrible shrieking from the lower levels  they heard their teammates calling for  help clearly distressed they weren't  even using their radios they just kept  screaming and yelling begging the others  to come down there and help them but as  the rest of the team descended into the  lower levels they soon realized that  they've been lowered into a trap by  beasts far more intelligent and  diabolical than they'd ever imagined  this was the story of the first time scp  foundation operatives ran into specimens  of scp-939  and lived to tell the tale in the  darkness below that abandoned warehouse  building they discovered a teeming den  of monsters large quadrupedal beasts  with translucent red skin and long  vicious spines streaking their back  trails of human flesh dangled from their  long fangs the monsters were standing  atop the corpses of the team members  who'd been calling for help moments  before or rather  seemed like they were calling for help  moments before the scp-939 instances had  borrowed the voices of their prey to  order a slightly more substantial dinner  from above one of the two most potent  abilities of scp-939 is their power to  mimic voices and do so with genuinely  terrifying accuracy it is currently  unknown to the foundation how exactly  they do this because 939 specimens don't  actually need to hear a voice before  they can imitate it and the complex  structure of their imitations and speech  patterns suggests a far greater level of  intelligence than their more  superficially bestial nature implies  theoretically you could hold an entire  conversation with a 939 behind a screen  door and have no idea that your  conversation partner was a creature that  would be just as happy to chew the head  off your neck as they would be to talk  to you speaking of which back to the  trapper team the survivors were cornered  by a gaggle of monsters using the voices  of their dead teammates the creatures  advanced with dripping [ __ ] preparing to  lunge and add another few bodies to the  count thankfully the survivors thought  fast opening fire and escaping out into  the hall as the creatures pursued after  a tense firefight and calling in a hefty  contingent of reinforcements from a  nearby containment site the trapper team  just barely got the situation under  control narrowly avoiding becoming just  another voice in the repertoire of this  particular 939 nest the foundation were  able to capture several viable specimens  and bring them in for containment and  study while some lives were lost the  monsters were caught but 939 stands  apart from the rest of the anomalous  crowd in a number of ways including the  fact that its true horrors were only  unleashed after containment the trapper  team that had fought tooth and nail to  apprehend the creatures in the first  place began to behave strangely during  debriefing despite their communication  devices recording a relatively clear  audio account of the incident the  survivors experienced odd lapses in  memory details that likely would have  been burned into the mind of anyone else  experiencing these events were  completely absent from the recollections  of the team members it was a phenomenon  the foundation had only seen once before  it was the exact kind of behavior  exhibited by people who have undergone  amnestic treatment it was this  comparison that led them to discovering  scp-939 second potent anomalous effect  they quite literally breathe a form of  aerosolized amnesic dubbed  amnc227 it inhibits the part of the  brain that allows people to form  memories for the duration of their  exposure to the gas creating a kind of  memory camouflage that 939 specimens are  able to hide in the gas is odorless  colorless and tasteless you could be  standing in a room full of it and never  even know they only tell that you'd ever  have memories erased by amn amnc227  is a strange sense of deja vu you'll  experience if you return to the point of  exposure it was an amnestic compound so  effective the foundation floated the  idea of using it for their own purposes  seeing as it's a lot easier to get amn  c227 from 939 than the usual method of  sacrifices to anatashisha from perfect  voice mimicry to impeccable memory  erasing with the added bonus of  intelligent pack hunting and an  exceedingly powerful bite strength 939  appeared to be a species of perfect  predators for luring in and killing  humans naturally the foundation had  questions chief among them being what  the hell are these things and how do  they work the more the foundation  experimented on scp-939  the more they became keenly aware of the  fact that these things don't operate  like any other living being almost all  of their internal systems from veins to  their digestive system are entirely  vestigial beneath their translucent skin  these monsters are effectively dead  nothing works and somehow nothing needs  to work they consume human flesh but the  flesh simply rots in their stomach until  they later vomited out nothing about  their biology explains how they produce  amnesics or how they even technically  survive one sample was fully dissected  it's different vital systems placed into  various tubes and the monsters still  tries to talk to foundation personnel as  they walk past its containment location  some of the creatures childish ranting  was recorded for posterity and the  recordings are nothing short of truly  chilling have you seen our pictures we  like drawing daddy hung them on the wall  except for sometimes when the others in  white coats took them away daddy told us  not to draw pictures like those they  made him sad so we did our best to draw  other things but sometimes we forgot  sometimes daddy hid the pictures or  ripped them up he told us that it wasn't  that he didn't like them he said it was  to keep us safe from the mean doctors in  the white coats but then the doctors  took daddy away  and some of the things said by this  dissected creature have been even more  disturbing we got so hungry it was bad  but we ate our old skin and our old head  it tasted good but it was still bad we  were still hungry after that and asked  for food they gave us food even our  favorites but none of it tasted right to  us all that tasted good was one piece of  meat we asked for more of that in hopes  of understanding their biology better  the foundation also decided to run some  samples through scp-914 the clockworks  as expected the coarse and rough  settings destroyed and deconstructed the  creature the data on the one-to-one  setting was redacted but most  frightening of all was the results of  the fine and very fine experiments for  the fine setting the creature simply  came back dead for the very fine setting  the creature had been reduced to a  smoldering pile of white ash the only  conclusion we can take from this is that  on a truly cosmic level 939 is meant to  be dead and just when you think that  scp-939 has hit the ceiling on true  horror the monsters continued to impress  by raising that nightmarish bar after 11  years in containment one of the 939  specimens gave birth to a litter of  infants this doesn't seem all that  horrifying seeing as being able to  reproduce would at least give 939  something in common with the rest of the  animal kingdom but the foundation were  horrified to find that the larval stage  of scp-939 looks pretty much identical  to a human baby researchers who were  ordered to dissect these creatures  finding out in the process that they  were identical to human infants on the  inside too were offered amnestics due to  the understandably traumatic nature of  the experience one of the births was  stillborn and the others quickly  cannibalized it the surviving beasts  soon learned to perfectly imitate the  voices and behavior of human children  offering yet another reason that you  cannot trust any of your senses when it  comes to scp-939  as they grew and matured the more human  parts simply fell off like a snake  shedding its skin after a period of  prolonged pain and discomfort more so  than most creatures the foundation  contains  scp-939's very existence is enough to  cause a sense of existential dread and  for a creature as full of surprises as  scp-939 of course there would be another  twist in the long red tail you see we  mentioned earlier that the scp  foundation briefly considered using amn  c227 the amnesic gas exhaled by 939  specimens as a form of class b amnestics  however this plan was later cancelled  when a horrifying side effect came to  light amnesia is never a good feeling  having complete blank spots in your  memory is actually extremely distressing  to experience and as we mentioned  earlier people exposed to amn c227 seem  to experience a palpable sense of deja  vu when they first experience it it'll  be mild but it'll slowly get stronger as  they move towards the source little by  little you'll feel satisfaction drawing  closer until you're wandering into a  deep dark cave and before you know it a  set of red jaws are closing around your  neck and it's all over that's right  amnc227 not only wipes the memories of  encounters with scp-939  it also lures any survivors back into  the lair of the creatures they've been  given the ketter class because there's a  whole species of these things and even  the foundation's best scientists can't  know for sure how far their habitats  extend they could be waiting for you  right now ready to call to you in a  friendly voice so remember kids don't  believe everything you hear after all  sounds can be deceiving now go check out  evil monster created by scp foundation  scp-2419 the laughing men and scp-002  the living room and the most terrifying  scp rooms for more terrifying scp  creatures
 

